euthydemus-learn.logic.r1: argue/two-senses: C (S17): "learning" is taken as grasping or understanding what is dictated, as the quick pupils do in C and as acquiring from teachers knowledge one does not yet have where learner is used else, a reader says
euthydemus-learn.logic.r1: argue/two-senses: C (S17): "unlearned" is taken as dull or slow, as opposed to the clever, quick pupils in C and as not knowing the things one is being taught where unlearned_k is used else, a reader says
